  7.3 "Answers remain in RAM" — measured, and it does not

  submit_answer embeds the student's claim in the demand description:
  f"...requires mathd-cli to verify student claim '{claim}' for question ...".
  The claim is built from the student's answer. The no-binary path therefore
  writes the answer to demands.jsonl.

  $ PYTHONPATH=novacore/src python f3-14-probes.py
  ### PROBE D: study session, does the student's answer reach disk?
  mathd_cli_path resolved to: None
  verdict: DemandLogged
  demand entry fields: ['created_at', 'description', 'entry_id', 'expected_sha256', 'instructions', 'item_type', 'status', 'target_filename', 'title', 'urls']
  token present in description: True
  token present in title:       False
  file written: demands.jsonl (831 bytes)

  test_answers_stay_in_ram_w5_privacy does not catch this because it looks for
  the answer in files other than the demand store; the demand store is the
  intended output of that code path, so the leak hides inside the feature.

  F3.14-F3 (finding): a student answer is persisted in the demand log,
