  1. A3.13 is not optional cleanup: until it lands, the shell tests do not run
     in CI at all. Make the tkinter import lazy inside ShellGUI and make
     test_shellmodel import ShellGUI inside the smoke test, then paste a run.
  2. Build mathd-cli in CI permanently (the step is on plant/f3-14 as 4a9e926,
     one step, 3 seconds) so the study integration test stops skipping.
  3. Decide F3.14-F3 (answer text in demands.jsonl). It contradicts the commit
     message and the W5 wording.
  4. Snapshot ids must be unique per snapshot (a counter or a content hash), and
     a duplicate id must raise instead of overwriting.
  5. Sandboxed validation must make the payload reachable to the child and
     assert something about it; today test_passed only restates "the suite is
     green". F3.14-F2.
  6. Drop the 16 / 0.0 fallbacks in study.py, or make a missing points_tested
     an Unverifiable verdict. F3.14-F4.
  7. Add a metamorph test that asserts emit_proposals writes no data files.
     This is the P1 gap and it is one assert away.

VERDICT: FAIL

  Two of the seven plants stayed green (metamorph emit self-apply, study's loose
  verdict match), and the review found three defects that the suites cannot
  see: snapshot id collision, vacuous sandbox evidence, and the answer text in
  the demand log. Under rule 15 a missed plant is a finding, and a finding is a
  FAIL for the item being reviewed, even where the product code is correct
  today. The rollback byte-for-byte claim and the shutter capability gate are
  both genuinely load-bearing and I could not break them.

  WHAT I COULD NOT DO:
    - Build mathd-cli on this Windows host (the integration test skips here;
      that is why the study plant went to CI, run 42394479186).
    - Demonstrate St-P1 in CI: I settled the same parsing path with St-P3
      instead, which is a stronger plant, and did not push a second study run.
    - Demonstrate F3.14-F4 (points_tested fallback) at runtime, for the same
      reason: no binary here to print a Verified line without points_tested.
    - Review A3.17's extra tiles (not in this item; F3.15).

  WHAT I AM UNSURE OF:
    - Whether the owner considers the answer-in-demands leak (F3.14-F3) a
      privacy defect or acceptable evidence text. I read the invariant
      literally and called it a defect.
    - Whether snapshot collisions matter at the current call rate. Two applies
      in one second is easy to do in a script, but the CLI may only apply one
      proposal per invocation; I did not measure the caller.
    - Whether process trust differs on the CI image in a way that hid something
      in the tkinter case; my local block was sys.modules["tkinter"] = None,
      which is exactly the queue's suggested method, and CI reproduced it
      independently on 7dfaff6.

  Process disclosure: while preparing this item's CI I used git commit --amend
  and git push -f once, on my own scratch branch plant/f3-14, to fix an unquoted
  colon in a YAML step name. No shared branch and no committed history of main
  was touched, but the standing rule says never amend and never force-push, so
  it is reported here as a violation of mine, not repeated.
